Hi [~accountid:63fe21787c30bbd6b33e09d3] 

Thanks for assisting with this, please see below the Licensor’s response in red:

C*lause 3.7* - Can you confirm that this clause means the Licensor has the right to move Bolt to another suite within the same building as opposed to another suite at a different location? -{color:#bf2600}Yes, within the same building (we are a standalone site so do not have any other properties).{color}

 

*Clause 3.9* - Can you please confirm what is the state that the Licensor requires here? -{color:#bf2600}We would ask that all customers leave an office as they found it, with the exception of fair wear and tear. As the office is unmanned then this clause should never be an issue even if you did move out.{color}

 

*Clause 3.13* - Can this clause be removed please as this clause is problematic and should be amended as you cannot exclude liability for death or personal injury caused by a party’s negligence, fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation and stated in the *Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977*.  -{color:#bf2600}We would not be happy to remove this clause entirely but what we can do is edit it slightly so that at the end we add on “….granted by this Licence, unless caused by negligent actions of the Licensor.” Obviously should death or injury be caused and we were found to be negligent/responsible then the law would override any clause in the Licence to Occupy anyway.{color}



*Clause 4.20* - Given the nature of this being an ‘unmanned office’ how often is the testing required -{color:#bf2600}If it is unmanned then this is not required to be done by you – as stated in the clause it is only “…in the event that there shall be five or more occupants of the Property at any one time….” You rarely have one occupant, let alone five, so you are not required to carry out any fire risk assessment of your own.{color}



Thanks

Hey [~accountid:5f17f7301084620015f4972a]

This insurance claim has nothing to do with Bolt as the issue here is between the passenger and the driver and Bolt is not a party to the incident. I would suggest advising them that the passenger has access to the journey information in the passengers app? (if this is not the case, please do correct me). 

See suggested response below: 



{color:#006644}_Dear (Insert name)_{color}

{color:#006644}_Thank you for your enquiry._ {color}

{color:#006644}_We understand that you have requested some additional information regarding a journey, we would guide you to locating this information in the Bolt App. If the Passenger would like to review information regarding a previous journey this information is all contained within the Bolt App under “My Trips”._ {color}

{color:#006644}_Please note, Bolt does not arrange insurance on behalf of any Driver. Drivers using the Bolt platform arrange their own insurance for their vehicles. In these circumstances and if you haven't done so already, you can use the registration plate of the vehicle to search for a vehicle's insurer's details at the Motor Insurance Database:_{color}[{color:#006644} +_https://www.askmid.com_+{color}|https://www.askmid.com/]{color:#006644} _._  {color}

{color:#006644}_From this website, you can submit a one-off search after which you will receive the policy number, name of insurers and contact details to help you progress any claim._  {color}

{color:#006644}_We trust that you will find this information useful._ {color}

{color:#006644}_Should you require any additional information, please do not hesitate to contact us._ {color}



